We need to produce corrected HTML file implementing all fixes. Let's enumerate bugs and required features.

1. Clear whole canvas in screen pixels each frame before transform. In draw(), we currently clear with fillRect(0,0,VIRTUAL_W,VIRTUAL_H) after setting transform? Actually we set fillRect before transform, using virtual units but canvas is in screen pixels (due to setTransform(dpr,...)). So need to clear full canvas: ctx.fillRect(0,0,canvas.width,canvas.height) before applying letterbox transform. Since ctx currently has transform set to dpr scaling, we can just clear with canvas.width/height. Then apply letterbox transform.

2. Font sizes: use virtual units (px) inside scaled transform. So replace '0.3vh' with e.g. '0.3px' (since virtual units are 1 = 1 unit). Use appropriate sizes: maybe 0.3 for bin labels, 0.5 for HUD. Ensure crisp.

3. Start screen appears: overlay should be shown initially with title, goal, controls. Currently overlay hidden. Need to set overlay content for start screen and show it. Also any key or click starts. Already keydown start triggers startGame. But overlay not shown. So set overlay.show initially and fill with start text. Also need to hide overlay when game starts.

4. Arrow keys: update checks keys['left'] etc but keydown stores e.key.toLowerCase() => 'arrowleft' not 'left'. Need to map arrow keys to 'left','right','down','up' or handle directly. Also handle Down arrow and S for lower. So in keydown, map e.key to appropriate keys: if e.key === 'ArrowLeft' set keys['left']; etc. Also 'a','d','s',' '.

5. Grabbed object stays in objects and moves. Need to remove from objects when grabbed, and have it move with gripper. So when gripper reaches object and grabs, we should set holdingObj and remove from objects array. Also its position should be relative to gripper (maybe store offset). We'll handle by setting holdingObj and removing from objects. Then during holding, object's x,y should follow gripper (draw uses gripper position). For drop, we need to spawn a falling object that moves down until lands.

6. Gripper lifts after grabbing: after grabbing, gripper should close, lift back up to gantry (gripperY back to up position). So after grab, set gripperState='lifting' maybe, and move gripperY up to upY (0.8). While lifting, cannot move? Could allow move but fine. After reaching up, set state='holding' (or 'up' with holdingObj). We'll implement state 'lifting' then 'holding'.

7. Dropping: object should fall straight down from gripper into bin or floor, scored when lands. So need a falling object state: when dropObject called, create a falling object with x = gripperX (center), y = gripperY + jawH + obj.h/2 (or similar), vy = 0, and then in update, move down with gravity until y reaches bin top or floor. Determine bin under x. If lands in bin and color matches, score; else lose life. Then remove object. Also need to handle if object falls off right end? Not relevant.

8. Lowering targets object at moment Space pressed; should grab whatever under jaws when they reach belt height. So we should not pre-select target; instead when gripper reaches belt height, check objects under jaws and grab if any. So remove target selection at press; just set gripperState='down', fastDrop false. When gripperY reaches belt level, check for object under jaws (within x range). If found, grab (remove from objects, set holdingObj). If not, go back up.

9. Clamp dt to 0.05.

10. On-screen buttons: handle pointerleave/pointercancel to stop movement. Also ensure pointerup outside button stops. We'll add listeners for pointerleave and pointercancel on buttons to set keys false.

11. HUD should show combo, lives as icons; win/lose overlay text correct; Restart button works from those screens. Already overlay shows "Press R to play again" static; need to change based on win/lose. Also need to show combo in HUD. Lives icons already there but maybe improve.

Additional: need to ensure start screen overlay shows title, goal, controls. Provide text.

Also need to ensure that when state is start, update/draw not run game logic. draw should still render background maybe but overlay covers.

Implement all.

Let's design code.

State machine: 'start','play','win','lose'.

Variables: gripperState: 'up','down','lifting','holding','dropping'? Actually dropping handled by falling object separate.

Holding object: holdingObj with its own x,y for drawing? We'll store holdingObj and when drawing gripper, draw object at gripper position.

When grab: remove from objects, set holdingObj, gripperState='lifting', targetY = upY (0.8). In update, if gripperState==='lifting', move gripperY up until reaches upY, then set gripperState='holding'.

When drop: create falling object: {x: gripperX, y: gripperY + jawH + holdingObj.h/2, w: holdingObj.w, h: holdingObj.h, color, shape, vy:0, falling:true}. Add to objects? Could have separate fallingObjects array. Simpler: add to objects with property falling true, and in update handle falling separately. But objects also move with belt; we don't want that. So separate array fallingObjects.

When dropObject called: determine bin under gripperX (using getBins). If correct bin, we still need to drop and then score when lands. So we can store intendedBin on falling object. When it lands, check.

Landing: floorY = VIRTUAL_H - 0.2? Actually bins sit on bottom edge. Floor is bottom of screen. We'll define floorY = VIRTUAL_H - 0.2 (just above bottom). If falling object's y + h >= floorY, then it lands. Determine bin: if x within bin range and bin top <= y? Actually bin top is bin.y. If object's bottom reaches bin.y + bin.h? Better: if object's y + h >= bin.y + bin.h (i.e., reaches bin bottom) and x within bin, then it's in bin. But simpler: when falling, check if x within bin and y + h >= bin.y + bin.h? Actually bin is at bottom, so object falls onto bin top (bin.y). So if object's y + h >= bin.y and x within bin, then it lands in bin. But we also need to ensure it doesn't pass through. We'll check when y + h >= bin.y (top of bin). Then if bin matches color, score; else lose life. If not over any bin, when y + h >= floorY (bottom), lose life.

After landing, remove falling object, clear holdingObj, set gripperState='up', gripperY=upY.

Also need to handle if object falls off right end? Not applicable.

Egg fast drop: if fastDrop and egg, break. We'll handle when gripper reaches belt and grabs egg with fastDrop true: break egg, lose life, spawn crack particles, no holding.

Fast drop detection: pressing Space twice quickly while lowering. We'll track lastSpace time and if second press within window, set fastDrop true.

Now implement.

Also need to ensure that when gripper is holding, it cannot move? Brief says after grabbing, lift back up, then can be moved to bin. So while lifting and holding, allow movement? Probably yes after lifted. We'll allow movement always.

